# The Voice-tab agent calls an OpenAI-compatible chat gateway. The browser
# can't call it directly (CORS), so the Vite dev server proxies /llm/* upstream
# and injects the key server-side — the key never ships to the browser.
# Copy this to `.env` and fill in your key.

# Server-side only (no VITE_ prefix = never exposed to the browser):
LLM_UPSTREAM=https://rootsys.cloud/v1
LLM_API_KEY=your-key-here

# Exposed to the browser (safe — just the model name):
VITE_LLM_MODEL=kimi-k2.7

# Where the Ruang WhatsApp bot's local API lives (for schedule sync + in-app
# invite approvals). Defaults to the bot's localhost port; only set this if you
# changed BOT_PORT in bot/.env or run the bot elsewhere.
# VITE_BOT_URL=http://localhost:8788

# Transcription needs NO key — it uses the browser's built-in speech
# recognition (Chrome/Edge). No Python sidecar.
#
# NOTE: the proxy only runs under `npm run dev`. For a static production
# build, put the gateway call behind a real backend instead.
